e=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center;"><figcaption class=3D"py-1">Fi=
gure 5</figcaption></div></figure>
<p>This method can eliminate collision; however, it is expensive to query t=
he database to check if a shortURL exists for every request. A technique ca=
lled bloom filters [2] can improve performance. A bloom filter is a space-e=
fficient probabilistic technique to test if an element is a member of a set=
. Refer to the reference material [2] for more details.</p>
<h4 id=3D"base-62-conversion">Base 62 conversion</h4>
<p>Base conversion is another approach commonly used for URL shorteners. Ba=
se conversion helps to convert the same number between its different number=
 representation systems. Base 62 conversion is used as there are 62 possibl=
e characters for <em>hashValue</em>. Let us use an example to explain how t=
he conversion works: convert 11157<sub>10</sub> to base 62 representation (=
11157<sub>10</sub> represents 11157 in a base 10 system).</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>From its name, base 62 is a way of using 62 characters for encoding. The=
 mappings are: <em>0-0, ..., 9-9, 10-a, 11-b, ..., 35-z, 36-A, ..., 61-Z, w=
here</em> =E2=80=98a=E2=80=99 stands for 10, =E2=80=98Z=E2=80=99 stands for=
 61, etc.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>11157<sub>10</sub>&nbsp;=3D 2 x 62<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+ 55 x 62<sup>1</sup=
> + 59 x 62<sup>0</sup>&nbsp;=3D&nbsp;[2, 55, 59] -&gt; [2, T, X] in base 6=
2 representation. Figure 6 shows the conversation process.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
;"><img alt=3D"Image represents a diagram illustrating the conversion of a =
decimal number (11157) into its base-62 representation.  The left side show=
s a repeated division process.  The number 11157 is repeatedly divided by 6=
